    <tei:body>
      <tei:div corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:prayer:eruv_tavshilin" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-rishon-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-one-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n12.jpg">
        <tei:p><tei:pb ed="1965" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-rishon-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-one-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n12.jpg" n="7"/><tei:milestone unit="prayer-part" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:prayer:eruv_tavshilin/blessing"/>Blessed art Thou, O Lord our God, King of the World, who has sanctified us with His commandments and given us the commandment of the Eruv. </tei:p>
        <tei:p><tei:milestone unit="prayer-part" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:prayer:eruv_tavshilin/declaration"/>Be it permitted, through this Eruv, to bake, to cook, to keep warm, to kindle a light and to prepare on the festival everything needed for the Sabbath, to us and to all who dwell in this town. <tei:milestone unit="prayer-part"/></tei:p>
      </tei:div>
    </tei:body>
